For each earlier finding, say whether the problem it describes is still in the code above.

- `fixed`: the code no longer has the problem. It may have been fixed on a different line, in a different way, or by moving the code. Say `fixed` only when you can point at the code that now handles it, or the problematic code is gone.
- `still_present`: the problem is still there.
- `unsure`: you cannot tell from this file alone, for example the fix may live in another file, or the part of the file that matters is cut off.
- Judge the code as it is now, not the wording of the finding. A finding's line number may no longer match.
- When you are not sure, answer `unsure`. Calling a real problem fixed is worse than leaving a fixed one marked unsure.

Respond with a JSON object: {"findings": [{"id": "<label of the finding>", "status": "fixed" | "still_present" | "unsure"}]} with one entry for every finding.
